  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47694\", \"PowerToys#23857\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. The closest match is PowerToys#47694, which covers the Power Display flyout. It is hard-coded to the bottom-right of the screen and ignores taskbar orientation. A maintainer replied that bottom-right placement is by design and reclassified it as a feature request. It is still open as a request, and I found no fix or workaround in it. PowerToys#23857 is the same complaint for the Quick Access tray flyout. It always opened in the lower-right corner whatever the taskbar position. It was marked as a duplicate of #23772 and was due a hotfix in 2023. That ticket predates native vertical taskbar support in Windows 11, so the behavior you see now may be a regression or a new gap. For now, expect both flyouts to open at the bottom-right. To get this changed, add your use case and a thumbs-up to #47694. If the Quick Access flyout is still wrong on your current version, say so there or in a new bug report.\"}",
